From: FP3 camera work
Subject: [PATCH] camera: a Face focus mode that finds and boxes a face

Adds a focus-mode dropdown (Continuous / Manual / Face) and, for Face, a
small dependency-free face detector - the PICO method, a cascade of
pixel-comparison trees, the algorithm behind the browser face finders - run
as a pipeline branch beside the QR-code detector. A found face is reported as
a signal and drawn as a box over the viewfinder. Windowing the autofocus onto
the face is left for later: that control is an array, which the PipeWire
libcamera node does not carry, so the focus stays the continuous whole-frame
one for now.

The trained cascade `facefinder` is copied in during prepare().
